~ start
cyrus: [#noportrait] Ah... The bells are ringing. I guess it’s about time for the Accolade. 
cyrus: It appears it’s a tale beyond time. Even the eldest don’t remember when the Dome came to be. Only that the sky used to look more beautiful, more... detailed. 
cyrus: It’s been around 30 years that the sky has become pixelated. And of course the governments don’t exactly give us a clear answer. Thankfully the Divine does a better job at it. 
cyrus: “The world is in danger. The Dome is there to protect you. But you will not need its protection forever. The Great Propagation will happen.” 
cyrus: Or at least that’s what a prophet said. Was it several? 
cyrus: Right, the Prophecy Miracle, when several prophets said the same words at the exact same time throughout the entire Dome.  
cyrus: Its name does it justice. They all replied with the exact same answers to everyone who would ask them. Questions asked in the north would be answered by prophets from all across the dome at the same time.
cyrus: And thus, even if the Divine sometimes guides in ways that oppose the governments, they can’t stop It, as the people trust It. 
cyrus: So, what? You may ask. There is a giant entity that just hovers everyone’s heads and controls the world? 
cyrus: The answer is, not exactly. And that’s why those bells ring right now. 
cyrus: The Hero has been declared. A young pure man of virtue, ready to lead his party under the direct guidance of the Divine. 
cyrus: That’s for who the Accolade is. Pretty big and important as you can guess. Almost everyone from around the Dome is here to observe it. 
cyrus: ... Almost everyone. 
 
cyrus: Some others instead... even though they could be basking in the glory of the moment... Have to run through the sewage...!
cyrus: It appears she lost me for now. I should have time to proceed carefully instead of continuing rushign on.
cyrus: ... This place is much quieter than usual.
=> END